--- initialize
{"id": 1, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "result": {"capabilities": {"completionProvider": {"triggerCharacters": ["."]}, "definitionProvider": true, "hoverProvider": true, "textDocumentSync": {"change": 1, "openClose": true, "save": {"includeText": false}}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "lume", "version": "0.5.0"}}}
--- a file with an error, then fixed
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [{"message": "unknown name `nope`\nhelp: names must be bound with `name = value` or `var name = value` before use", "range": {"end": {"character": 11, "line": 1}, "start": {"character": 7, "line": 1}}, "severity": 1, "source": "lume"}], "uri": "<tmp>/one/hello.lume"}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [], "uri": "<tmp>/one/hello.lume"}}
--- a module, checked through the main.lume that imports it
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [{"message": "`*` cannot combine an `Int` and a `Str`", "range": {"end": {"character": 34, "line": 0}, "start": {"character": 33, "line": 0}}, "severity": 1, "source": "lume"}], "uri": "<tmp>/mods/helper.lume"}}
--- a module of a package, unsaved text
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [{"message": "`hi` returns `Str`, but this is an `Int`\nhelp: write `\"#{42}\"` or `42.to_s`", "range": {"end": {"character": 22, "line": 0}, "start": {"character": 20, "line": 0}}, "severity": 1, "source": "lume"}], "uri": "<tmp>/pkg/util.lume"}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [], "uri": "<tmp>/pkg/util.lume"}}
--- the module fixed again
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [], "uri": "<tmp>/mods/helper.lume"}}
--- hover and go to definition
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [], "uri": "<tmp>/mods/nav.lume"}}
a local                        hover "ann: Person" | definition <tmp>/mods/nav.lume:12:3
a var                          hover "var later: Person" | definition <tmp>/mods/nav.lume:13:7
a parameter                    hover "by: Int" | definition <tmp>/mods/nav.lume:9:22
a function                     hover "def older(p: Person, by: Int) -> Person" | definition <tmp>/mods/nav.lume:9:5
a constructor                  hover "struct Person\n  name: Str\n  age: Int" | definition <tmp>/mods/nav.lume:3:8
a method                       hover "def Person.greet -> Str" | definition <tmp>/mods/nav.lume:7:7
a field                        hover "Person.name: Str" | definition <tmp>/mods/nav.lume:4:3
a field read bare in a method  hover "Person.name: Str" | definition <tmp>/mods/nav.lume:4:3
a built-in method              hover "Str.upcase -> Str" | definition None
a function of another module   hover "def helper.twice(n: Int) -> Int" | definition <tmp>/mods/helper.lume:1:9
--- completion while typing: the file does not parse, the last check is used
puts later.        -> name, age, greet
puts helper.       -> twice
puts later.name.   -> len, empty?, to_int, to_float, upcase, downcase, trim, lines, split, chars, contains?, starts_with? ...
puts la            -> offers ann, later, older, Person, helper, def, while
--- generators and interfaces (milestones 70-77)
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [], "uri": "<tmp>/mods/seq.lume"}}
a generator                    hover "def naturals -> Iterator[Int]" | definition <tmp>/mods/seq.lume:11:5
a generator held in a var      hover "var g: Iterator[Int]" | definition <tmp>/mods/seq.lume:18:7
next on it                     hover "Iterator[Int].next -> Int?" | definition None
a generator default            hover "def Bag.doubled -> Iterator[Int]" | definition <tmp>/mods/seq.lume:3:7
puts g.            -> offers next, take, filter, to_list, zip
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", "params": {"diagnostics": [{"message": "`main` hands out items with `yield`, so it gives `Iterator[T]`\nhelp: say what it gives: `def main(...) -> Iterator[Int]:`, with the type its `yield`s have", "range": {"end": {"character": 3, "line": 16}, "start": {"character": 0, "line": 16}}, "severity": 1, "source": "lume"}], "uri": "<tmp>/mods/seq.lume"}}
--- a request it does not answer, then shutdown
{"error": {"code": -32601, "message": "`textDocument/rename` is not supported"}, "id": 35, "jsonrpc": "2.0"}
{"id": 36, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "result": null}
exit: 0
